{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world","id":597203,"title":"People Refusing to try new world","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-20T13:29:24-07:00","id":597203,"title":"People Refusing to try new world","content":"I keep meeting so many people who refuses to try new world of darkness and they always just say that the new world of darkness is broken because its too complicated or they tell me old world is deeper or made more sense.. Maybe some one can explain to me how its so complicated ?'<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T14:08:53-07:00","id":597304,"title":"","content":"It's really not. The system is actually much more streamlined than CWoD. And what they are mistaking for CWoD being &quot;deeper&quot; is that NWoD doesn't have a metaplot and is intended as a toolbox, where setting elements are chosen by the ST to suit the needs of the story. A lot of the most common complaints I've heard from people who refuse to try NWoD are founded on misinformation (unsurprisingly, since it's hard to be well-informed on a game you haven't actually played.)<br /> <br /> This is also one of those topics that tends to result in flame wars, so I'm going to keep an eye on this thread. I hope we can have a civil conversation about the differences between the two WoDs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T14:15:24-07:00","id":597311,"title":"","content":"Most of the CWoD games have been around a little over, or a little under 20 years. People learned them in their youth, and keep playing them because they already know them. Sitting and reading a new 400+ page book and setting with splat books is just too time consuming for many people these days. The hobby of Role Playing is waning in general, it's just how things go. There's all sorts of things for people to do with their free time now that don't requiring syncing ever busy schedules for 6+ hours a week. So role playing is a high investment low reward kind of hobby when people tend to flake more and more, or simply don't have time given real world circumstance.<br /> <br /> My point is, people are refusing new world cause they plain already know old world. The people who can make time just to play a game (which is already a hell of a commitment today) don't also want to learn new systems for the most part. Especially when it comes to niche games. World of Darkness is great, but it's far from the main stream in terms of RPGs. It's easier to find a new gaming group of high schoolers than it is to find an old timers group. Those kids have the time do pick up the books and read them and get invested. However very few kids are doing that compared to the 90s. So all in all. Unless you want to play DnD with teenagers, finding any roleplaying group seems to be pretty hard.<br /> <br /> Those hard core enough to keep up with it all often turn to online mediums these days to find the rare like minded individuals. Check roll20 sometime and you might get lucky. Sometimes those people turn to play by post, which is easier to plug into a busy day to day, but is ultimately generally fairly slow paced. Check rpol. A local gaming store might help, but they're fewer and far between. Sometimes you can post LFG add there though.<br /> <br /> I would argue NWoD is no less hard to get into than CWoD, but why learn something new when you already invested the time learning the old stuff back in your youth. I think that's most people's general point of view. I have tons of gamer friends who can't manage to work together to get a game going, and when the scheduling does work out, we bust out our old favorites for ease of play. I've practically given up expecting anyone to read new books. The only game I will run is Star Wars or DnD cause everyone who is a geek or roleplayer already knows the setting, themes, and moods.<br /> <br /> The only other advice I can give you is to check to see if there's a local chapter of the Camarilla or Minds Eye Society or whatever it's called these days in your area. There are LARPers who love all these games, and they will play with you, but my experiences with the Cam LARPs have been overall negative, but you might find a table top group that way.<br /> <br /> Lastly I will say this. And I don't mean to offend anyone. Finding new players is often a total crapshoot as well, as for every okay role player you find (AKA, someone who likes to game like you do). You find at least one person who isn't in it for the same thing you are, and you find one person with limited social skills who does not mesh well with a mostly social game at all. Finding a working cohesive group of people to sync schedules and RP together is insanely hard without it all blowing up over conflicts of personality and game style.<br /> <br /> All that said, I wish you luck,<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Mark","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 07-20-2015, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T14:22:47-07:00","id":597316,"title":"","content":"@MrMarkers Makes me wonder about the ages of both games fanbase. I was in my teens when it was at its height of popularity, but never really got into old World of Darkness. A lot of people on the new World of Darkness boards seem to be younger than myself, but clearly not all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-20-2015, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T14:35:08-07:00","id":597326,"title":"","content":"@nofather, My general impression is that the LARP community is mostly in their 30s+ and those are the dire hards for both CWoD and NWoD. On a tabletop level however, mostly it's younger 20 somethings who are more into drama than stabbing who move away from DnD into NWoD. Whereas the old school table toppers are still playing CWoD in one form or another. It's a broad generalization, but seems to be pretty accurate when I talk to people, and I've spent a large amount of time in the local friendly local gaming store, as my friend owns it and I've quasi worked there off and on for about 8 years now. I've also worked a booth at GenCon for a few years and this was the impression I got, which should be the epicenter of the hobby and give a pretty good sample size to make that judgement over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 07-20-2015, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T15:07:10-07:00","id":597364,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that assessment seems accurate, in broad strokes. I am in my mid-20s, discovered WoD in my late teens and at went to a Cam Requiem LARP at my college, didn't care for it but met someone there who was part of a private LARP troupe and invited me to join them and see if I liked it better. Fell in love with the game, been a diehard NWoD fan ever since, though now that I'm out of college I don't LARP much any more, and with MES not wanting to make MET rules for the NWoD 2nd Edition, I've pretty much switched to exclusively tabletop. Impossible to find time to run games any more though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T16:38:59-07:00","id":597492,"title":"","content":"Ah I've only gotten into Roleplaying games for the past 6 years or so. I've got a Sunday real life group I can play games with. I've been looking for so long to get a new world of darkness game going for long term but its so hard to find GM's. The first game I got into was Scion. <br /> <br /> I just love reading in general and now that I'm 25. I still love reading so I spend hours reading world of darkness stuff and can't find any GM's (I wish I could find some one who could run Demon the Decent for me). Hmmm as a matter of fact I've never had anyone GM a world darkness game for me that did not last more then 3 days. hmmmm. <br /> <br /> I've never tried larping but I will check that out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T19:03:14-07:00","id":597657,"title":"","content":"I cannot understand hating one WoD and loving a different one. Especially Vampire, which are different enough to have their own identities but still more similar than different.<br /> <br /> They are both Urban Fantasy/Horror games with several of the same types of critters just different slants of the mythology. For a systems monkey you can even mix and match your favorite versions easily if you so chose.<br /> <br /> The only one I understood at all was Dreaming players disliking Lost because it was triggery. Okay, I will give you that. I love both games a lot though, even if I do prefer Lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T04:55:51-07:00","id":598161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world#post597203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe some one can explain to me how its so complicated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Without any knowledge of the individual making the claim, my instinct is to dismiss such complaint as a smoke screen thrown up by people who don't want to admit they dislike the World of Darkness for no other reason than that it is not the old World of Darkness. When someone comes along to explain his position, I will exempt that person from this stereotype according to his explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:30:10-07:00","id":598441,"title":"","content":"Well player was telling me that the dice rolls are much more complicated then old world. That in old world they just had a threshold and rolled and if they pass it then they did there action. He mostly ranted about mage. <br /> <br /> I've tried explaining that new world is a toolbox that lets you use the meta from old world if you wish but they never really listen to me. <br /> <br /> <br /> Right now my favorite line so far is Demon the Decent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T09:53:06-07:00","id":598457,"title":"","content":"That seems a bit off. He might have gotten them confused.<br /> <br /> In old World of Darkness you have a threshold that changes. In new World of Darkness, outside of special circumstances, the threshold is always 8.<br /> <br /> Put down simply, almost every roll is Attribute + Skill + or - Modifiers, which may include other stats like Renown or a Discipline, countered against a target's Defense as a - modifier and so forth.<br /> <br /> 8, 9, or 10, you've got a success. If you have a 10, you roll again. If you get 5 successes, you've generally got an Exceptional Success, possibly for some added benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T11:40:47-07:00","id":598580,"title":"","content":"Yeah it sounds like your player might have their WoDs mixed up. In OWoD each task has a &quot;difficulty&quot; which is the number you need to roll or beat to get a success, and some tasks also have a minimum number of successes required. So for example, one roll might be difficulty 6 and require 3 successes, which means you'd need to get 6 or higher on at least three dice. On another, you might only need one success, but have a difficulty of 9, so if you roll at least one 9 or 10, you succeed. In NWoD, the &quot;difficulty&quot; and the required number of successes are fixed, you always need an 8 or higher to get a success, and you only ever need one success on a roll to succeed. You adjust the difficulty of a roll with bonus dice and dice penalties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T19:28:28-07:00","id":598930,"title":"","content":"There are still times when number of successes matter. It's ST discretion for some tasks, that mechanic hasn't been entirely eliminated","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T19:50:53-07:00","id":598952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world?p=598930#post598930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are still times when number of successes matter. It's ST discretion for some tasks, that mechanic hasn't been entirely eliminated</div> </div> </div> </div>Number of successes matters in certain contexts, like extended actions, contested actions, and things like combat where there are incremental degrees of success (more damage, etc.) And, of course, there's always ST discretion, but by the same token an ST could use their discretion to alter the target number to get a success if they wanted to. I've also heard Mummy plays with target number of successes, but I haven't played Mummy myself. Still, &quot;one success is all you need&quot; is the baseline assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-21-2015, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T06:53:52-07:00","id":607810,"title":"","content":"What worse is the fact that no matter how I explain it to them they just wave me off saying old world is better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T07:05:16-07:00","id":609359,"title":"","content":"For me when I first picked up the nWoD stuff (Main book and Requiem), compared to my massive oWoD collection, there were some quite marked differences which made me have a &quot;Eh?&quot;; Mostly;<ul><li>The obvious format changes from quite stark black-on-white to having background textures and generally being more &quot;pretty&quot;.</li> <li>Rules changes - It seemed like a lot had been removed (&quot;Where's the flaws....?&quot;)</li> <li>Complete lack of &quot;concrete&quot; mythology; in so much as everyone I knew took it as fact that in the oWoD there was, for definite, a &quot;Cain&quot; that Kindred descended from, whereas nWoD was all a bit shruggy and seemed to hint that some Clans had hugely different origins and no shared genesis.</li> <li>An extra level of social/faction type play with the Covenants, along with Clan and Sect (In that they'd all changed too so peoples default choice/s of cWoD factions/Clans etc weren't there).</li> <li>The very &quot;Hands off&quot; approach where as cWoD had been very much &quot;Hands on&quot;.</li> </ul><br /> Now I did say &quot;..when I first picked up ...&quot; as I didn't do anything with them for years. Collected the main splats but didn't even really read 'em and when I did I got a headache (Mage especially and I still don't &quot;get&quot; it, then again I don't get &quot;themes&quot; and all that jargon ... just play a cool game, s'bout all the depth I look for, depth comes from specific plots for me, not in exploring themes and motifs and those sorts of things!). My gaming group, IRL, still won't touch nWoD with a barge-pole. I keep raising it, asking, but they (To a player) refuse. Some of them have read parts of the new stuff even but still won't so it's not for lack of trying and their lack of exposure. Online I've really enjoyed it, what I've played and what has kept going. I know of other groups locally who likewise don't play nWoD and only play cWoD - then again they also don't come on here and probably still don't know of Onyx Paths existence...<br /> <br /> I think, for me at least, the nWoD is a tool kit and sand box where I <i>want</i> to include everything (Hence new splats get me all &quot;But how can I intergrate 'em when they didn't exist before? ARGH!&quot;) as it's my nature to collect all-the-things and use 'em all. The cWoD felt like a lot of the later lines were either limited or geographically unimportant to me (KotE in the middle of the UK? Yeah, probably don't need to worry about them!) so I could stick to Vamps, Weres, Ghosts, Changelings and Magi ... with bog standard mortals as hunters all as the default setting types. Then HtR came along and I managed to drop that in as the big-new-event in the WoD being their return to the world. Demon ... meh. Already had demonic entities and completely ignored using that line truth be told. Mummy was something that got used once I think.<br /> <br /> Compare that to the nWoD where it feels like all things are everywhere, all the time, and I feel like I have to at least factor everything into my head-canon for a setting even if it's just a Vampire game for example. I know I don't have too and likely I shouldn't, but I do. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/907-jay","name":"Jay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar907_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T10:16:37-07:00","id":609670,"title":"","content":"I prefer cWoD over nWoD purely for memory-related reasons. I know cWoD mechanics. If combat breaks out, I rarely need to open a book to see what a discipline or gift does what. I know the base mechanics, can quote them on the fly, and focus more time on telling the story than looking up stuff.<br /> <br /> I know if I were to play nWoD often enough I'd probably like it just as much, but since everyone I play with still uses cWoD games, it hasn't happened. I don't hate the nWoD itself and have nothing against it, but I'll always choose the familiar over the new when it comes to my hobbies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T12:29:49-07:00","id":609828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world?p=609670#post609670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer cWoD over nWoD purely for memory-related reasons. I know cWoD mechanics. If combat breaks out, I rarely need to open a book to see what a discipline or gift does what. I know the base mechanics, can quote them on the fly, and focus more time on telling the story than looking up stuff.<br /> <br /> I know if I were to play nWoD often enough I'd probably like it just as much, but since everyone I play with still uses cWoD games, it hasn't happened. I don't hate the nWoD itself and have nothing against it, but I'll always choose the familiar over the new when it comes to my hobbies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is at the heart of the issue. For most people, it's a matter of familiarity, be that with the mechanics or the setting or the metaplot, or what have you. Learning a new game is a significant investment of time and energy, and if you already love one game about vampires (or whatever), it hardly seems worth the effort to learn another game about vampires that you may or may not enjoy as much.<br /> <br /> I'm actually the same way, coming from the other direction. I learned NWoD first and at this point know Requiem so well I could play it without any books, as long as there aren't too many obscure bloodlines in play (At least with 1st Edition; still getting there with 2nd Edition, but it probably won't be long). I've got nothing against CWoD, in fact there are parts of it I think look really cool. But most of the time I'd rather play the game I'm more familiar with, and since all of my friends are in pretty much the same boat, we'll basically alway pick NWoD over CWoD.<br /> <br /> What can be frustrating is when people try to justify their preference by making it out to be superior to the alternative. Especially because the complaints people raise (about either game) are usually misconceptions. &quot;I don't need to try [thing I am unfamiliar with] to know [thing I am familiar with] is better&quot; is an all too common sentiment, unfortunately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:41:20-07:00","id":610039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world#post597203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I keep meeting so many people who refuses to try new world of darkness and they always just say that the new world of darkness is broken because its too complicated or they tell me old world is deeper or made more sense.. Maybe some one can explain to me how its so complicated ?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit for me are way more complicated in NWoD than OWoD.<br /> <br /> They are in the shadow but if they wanna affect stuff in the material world first they gotta go into the twilight and then fester which i still dont get how much time it take. The a couple of condition have to happen during festering for the spirit to be able to affect stuff in the material world but there are power that bypass that or maybe not. <br /> <br /> And there are 3 planes. Material, twilight and Shadow and the DM in games like Mage has to keep track of the 3. I had a game in which i had this perfectly good &quot;dungeon&quot; that was bypass by a a mage going into the twilight which was empty. I just preffer 2 planes, Material and umbra, the empty twilight never sat right with me.<br /> <br /> <br /> I started with RPGs with NWoD Forsaken and for a long time i didnt touch OWoD with a pole because i deemed too over the top. But i remember talking to this group of OWoD rabbid fans that told me that NWoD was worse because they recycle names from OWoD. For example &quot;gnosis is a stat from werewolf but now is from mage? Pftt thats cheap recycling&quot; that is the exact example they use along with something about malkavians and brujah i think.<br /> <br /> Personally I preffer OWoD, is no perfect but the probabilities in NWoD for sucess always seem off to me. The exploding dice could give you wildly different results and dramatic failures are so uncommon that only 1 in 7 years i witness one......and it was glorious.<br /> <br /> Setting wise i do preffer OWoD because i like its setting more but i prefer working around stablished setting than tool boxes. <br /> <br /> However in my country OWoD is by default more liked than NWoD for 2 reasons. First the whole OWoD line was translated into spanish while NWod only the cores and some of vampire i think. And secondly, i live in a racially insensitive country and thus many of the things OWoD is critize with dont fly here. I have seeing LFGs of WoD gypsies games for example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T15:55:38-07:00","id":610052,"title":"","content":"Twilight isn't a plane, it's a state of matter. You don't say something is &quot;in the twilight&quot; because there is no such thing as &quot;the twilight.&quot; You say it is &quot;in twilight&quot; which is basically just another way of saying it's phased out. A spirit in twilight is in the physical world, it's just out of phase with normal matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:13:01-07:00","id":610070,"title":"","content":"I always though while in twilight you could see nor interact with living things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T16:50:16-07:00","id":610117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world?p=610070#post610070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always though while in twilight you could see nor interact with living things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, cause you're out of phase. But you're <i>in</i> the physical world, you're just invisible and can't touch anything else in it. You know, like a ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T17:10:06-07:00","id":610164,"title":"","content":"Im confuse here, what the difference then? When in twilight a character is in the same spot that he was before just that the world look bleaker (maybe), there is no people and you can go through walls? <br /> <br /> And still, my minor issue is that is kinda overcomplicated for spirit as they have a set of rule for what they can and cannot do from The shadow to affect the material world but first they gotta be in the twilight but in there they can only use certain things and no other abilities and there is the whole festering thing that is a whole process on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-31-2015, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:17:08-07:00","id":610215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world?p=610164#post610164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im confuse here, what the difference then? When in twilight a character is in the same spot that he was before just that the world look bleaker (maybe), there is no people and you can go through walls?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's people. You might be thinking of the Shadow, but that's a different world entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And still, my minor issue is that is kinda overcomplicated for spirit as they have a set of rule for what they can and cannot do from The shadow to affect the material world but first they gotta be in the twilight but in there they can only use certain things and no other abilities and there is the whole festering thing that is a whole process on their own. </div> </div> </div>Sort of. Spirits have rules to be able to interact across the worlds. They also have rules for how they act in our world. One of those rules is that, automatically, when they enter our world, it's in a state of Twilight. It's not really that complicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-31-2015, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T18:26:01-07:00","id":610230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world?p=610164#post610164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im confuse here, what the difference then? When in twilight a character is in the same spot that he was before just that the world look bleaker (maybe), there is no people and you can go through walls?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you're in the same spot, everything looks exactly the same, only you are invisible and can't physically interact with anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world?p=610164#post610164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And still, my minor issue is that is kinda overcomplicated for spirit as they have a set of rule for what they can and cannot do from The shadow to affect the material world but first they gotta be in the twilight but in there they can only use certain things and no other abilities and there is the whole festering thing that is a whole process on their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no &quot;in there.&quot; Twilight is not a place. A spirit can cross from the shadow (the spirit world) into the flesh (the physical world) through various means. When they are in the physical world, they are not solid and they are invisible. The name for this state of being invisible and intangible is &quot;twilight.&quot; A spirit that is invisible and intangible (or, &quot;in twilight&quot;) can still interact with the physical world that it inhabits through various means such as numina (the name for spirit powers). Under certain conditions, a spirit in twilight can become visible and tangible. This is called &quot;manifesting.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T04:36:38-07:00","id":610658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world?p=610230#post610230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you're in the same spot, everything looks exactly the same, only you are invisible and can't physically interact with anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> There's no &quot;in there.&quot; Twilight is not a place. A spirit can cross from the shadow (the spirit world) into the flesh (the physical world) through various means. When they are in the physical world, they are not solid and they are invisible. The name for this state of being invisible and intangible is &quot;twilight.&quot; A spirit that is invisible and intangible (or, &quot;in twilight&quot;) can still interact with the physical world that it inhabits through various means such as numina (the name for spirit powers). Under certain conditions, a spirit in twilight can become visible and tangible. This is called &quot;manifesting.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ahh gotcha, i always understood it wrong then. Thanks for the clarification <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T18:12:37-07:00","id":622960,"title":"","content":"for me it was how clans were arranged in NWoD that turned me off about it<br /> <br /> beast though is starting to peek my interest and make me want to play a game, promethean always looked fun too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T16:07:31-07:00","id":624703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dezeroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/597203-people-refusing-to-try-new-world?p=622960#post622960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for me it was how clans were arranged in NWoD that turned me off about it</div> </div> </div> </div>What is off-putting about the way they are arranged? Just the fact tha they are sort of archetypes instead of factions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}